## Intensity curve (Street Dog Salon → Orbit)

Source pattern: Street Dog Salon Video #1 — DECLARE → ASSESS → ISOLATE → PROCESS (valley) → BUILD → REVEAL (highest peak). Script energy like “Today we [verb] [number] [subject]”. **Orbit adapts the shape; do not copy their 60s / 6-phase clock onto Shorts.** Intensity must **finish higher than it started**.

### Shorts (22–27s only — never stretch to 60s)

1. **DECLARE (0–1s):** strange picture on screen + punch. Not Orbit. Concrete, like “not one sun” / “planets made of diamond”.
2. **ASSESS (next few seconds):** one hard fact or measurement. Not poetry.
3. **REVEAL (last 4s + loop):** return to the same picture. Thursday film title on screen. “watch the full film →”. The last beat is the **highest intensity**, not a fade.
4. **Do not** add a long PROCESS valley with 10–12 cuts. That is how we get ≥40s Shorts.

### Longs (NOW **7–9 min** · expand later)

Stage lock (small channel, films ~1–9 views, ~3:14 avg hold on 21-min lives): **new longs target 7–9 minutes.** Pattern: Last Star (~8:37) · Europa (~9 min). Live 21-min Alien Worlds / Black Hole / Fermi are **not** the length to copy. Expand to 15–20–30 only after an 8-min film gets real impressions **and** hold stays past ~5 min. Do **not** hit 7–9 by chopping a 21-min lecture in half. Recut = new id if a live film is shortened.

1. Same curve over the film: **declare** on the picture (first 3s) → **assess**/stakes by 15s → **isolate** a first peak → **process** valley is where the **world** teaches (Orbit **ACTS** only in 1–2 inquisitive beats, not hover wallpaper) → **build** → **reveal** is the last 10s picture hold (highest image, Studio end screens). Never end on a baked subscribe card.
2. Intensity must finish higher than it started.
3. Still one strange world. Picture-first 3s. No baked subscribe. No brand sting.

